title: Sebastian Cox
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N9pHyf84DCc

British furniture designer and maker. He builds from coppiced hazel and British-grown hardwood, and his studio works to keep British woodland managed by giving its timber somewhere to go.

Maker of the [[Products of Silviculture Suent chair]]. The thin hazel rods keep their bark, so the chair still looks like the woodlot it came from.

He says wood is "made of solid carbon dioxide" and has a "massive impact on locking up carbon." (//The Radical Act of Environment//, Harewood Biennial, 2021)

The studio sells a 10-year guarantee and a refinishing service with the furniture. He is also plain about the catch: this work takes time and skill, and it costs more.

